# 17. Suggested Presentation Explanation

You can explain the project to the examiner like this:

Good morning/afternoon. Our project is titled “EduGenie – Google Gemini Powered Learning Assistant.”

EduGenie is an AI-powered educational platform designed to provide students with personalized learning assistance.

The main idea of our project is to combine conversational AI with learning activities such as explanations, summarization, quizzes, study planning, and progress tracking.

First, I will log into the EduGenie application.

After login, we can see the dashboard. From here, students can access the AI Tutor, Quiz Generator, Study Planner, and Progress modules.

Now I will demonstrate the AI Tutor. I will ask EduGenie, “Explain binary search to me as a beginner.”

The request is sent from the frontend to our backend. The backend constructs the appropriate prompt and communicates with the Gemini API. Gemini generates the response, and EduGenie displays the result to the student.

One important feature is that the explanation can be adapted to the student's learning level. If I change the level from beginner to advanced, the response can contain more technical details.

Next, I will demonstrate the quiz feature. I select Computer Science, Data Structures, Intermediate difficulty, and five questions. EduGenie generates a quiz based on these parameters.

After answering the questions, I submit the quiz. The system calculates the result and records the learning activity.

Now I can open the Progress section. It displays the student's learning activity and quiz performance.

Finally, I will demonstrate the Study Planner. I provide the subjects, available study time, and examination date. EduGenie generates a structured study schedule.

Therefore, the complete learning process supported by EduGenie is:

Learn, Practice, Evaluate, and Improve.

The project demonstrates how Google Gemini can be integrated into an educational application to provide interactive and personalized learning assistance.

