# 20. Questions the Examiner May Ask

### Q1. Why did you choose Gemini?

**Answer:**

> "Gemini provides generative AI capabilities that can be integrated into our application to support natural-language educational interactions, content generation, summarization, and other learning assistance features."

### Q2. What is the role of the backend?

> "The backend manages business logic, validates requests, communicates with the database, constructs AI requests, and securely communicates with Gemini."

### Q3. Why should the Gemini API key not be placed in the frontend?

> "Exposing the API key in client-side code could allow unauthorized users to obtain and misuse the credential. Therefore, AI API communication should be handled through a secure backend."

### Q4. What happens if Gemini is unavailable?

> "The application handles the failure and displays an appropriate error message rather than allowing the application to crash."

### Q5. How does EduGenie personalize learning?

> "The application can use information such as the student's selected learning level, topic, learning history, and study requirements when constructing learning requests and recommendations."

### Q6. Can Gemini always be trusted?

> "No. Generative AI can produce incorrect or incomplete information. Therefore, EduGenie should treat AI output as learning assistance and encourage verification for important academic information."

### Q7. What is the main advantage of your project?

> "EduGenie combines AI-based explanations with practice, planning, and progress features rather than functioning only as a general chatbot."

### Q8. What are the future enhancements?

> "Potential enhancements include voice interaction, image-based learning, multilingual support, advanced document learning, teacher dashboards, gamification, and more adaptive learning capabilities."

